@startuml
' Figure 3.4 - Sequence Diagram, Order Submission and Recipe Deduction
'
' Rebuilt in PlantUML. The mermaid version could not be sized: mermaid 11 ignores
' sequence options from both a %%{init}%% directive and mmdc -c, so actorMargin,
' messageMargin and every font size were inert - it rendered at a fixed 16px in a
' 1863-unit viewBox, which is 3.6pt on the page. PlantUML honours them.
'
' IngredientRepository and InventoryLedgerService are folded into RecipeDeduction as
' self-calls, named in the adjacent notes. Printed size is fontSize x 417.6 / canvas
' width, and canvas width is the sum of the lifeline columns, so two fewer columns is
' the single biggest gain available. Message labels are kept short for the same reason;
' the detail lives in the notes, which are anchored "over" a pair of lifelines and
' therefore cannot widen the canvas.
'
' Verified against OrderService.submitOrder, RecipeDeductionService.deductForOrder /
' handlePostDeductionThresholds and InventoryAlertService.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam defaultFontSize 26
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.8

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37474F
  ArrowFontSize 25
  ParticipantFontSize 26
  ParticipantFontStyle bold
  ParticipantPadding 16
  BoxPadding 12
  LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  GroupHeaderFontSize 25
  GroupHeaderFontStyle bold
  GroupBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  GroupBorderColor #2E7D32
}
skinparam note {
  FontSize 23
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  BorderColor #F9A825
}

hide footbox

title Sequence Diagram — Order Submission and Recipe Deduction Engine

participant "Waiter\n(POS UI)"   as W  #BBDEFB
participant "Order\nController"  as C  #E3F2FD
participant "Order\nService"     as OS #C8E6C9
participant "Recipe\nDeduction"  as RD #FFE0B2
participant "Event\nPublisher"   as EP #DCEDC8
participant "Inventory\nAlert"   as AL #FFCCBC

W  -> C  : 1. POST /orders
C  -> OS : 2. submitOrder(...)

group Single @Transactional boundary — steps 3 to 18
  OS -> OS : 3. open table
  note over OS, RD
    tableService.openTableForOrder
    SELECT … FOR UPDATE on the
    table row, status → OCCUPIED
  end note
  OS -> OS : 4. find customer
  note over OS, RD
    customerRepository.
    findByPhoneNumber — creates a
    Walk-in customer if unknown
  end note
  OS -> OS : 5. read menu item
  note over OS, RD
    an unavailable item is rejected
    before any stock moves
  end note

  OS -> RD : 6. deductForOrder
  note over OS, RD
    @Transactional(REQUIRED) —
    joins the caller's transaction
  end note
  RD -> RD : 7. read recipes
  note over RD, EP
    recipeRepository.findByMenuItemId
    required qty summed per ingredient
  end note
  RD -> RD : 8. lock rows
  note over RD, EP
    ingredientRepository.
    findAllByIdForUpdate — SELECT …
    FOR UPDATE in ascending id order,
    blocks concurrent transactions
  end note
  RD -> RD : 9. validate stock
  note over RD, EP #FFCDD2
    any shortfall raises
    InsufficientStockException → HTTP 409,
    whole transaction rolls back
  end note
  RD -> RD : 10. compute stock
  RD -> RD : 11. save ingredient
  RD -> RD : 12. ledger write
  note over RD, EP
    inventoryLedgerService.
    recordRecipeDeduction — one
    append-only row per ingredient
  end note
  RD -> EP : 13. item disabled
  note over RD, EP
    only when the ingredient reached zero
  end note
  RD -> RD : 14. reorder event
  RD --> OS : 15. complete
  OS -> OS : 16. save(order) — PENDING
  OS -> EP : 17. new ticket
  OS -> EP : 18. table status
end

note over OS, EP #E8F5E9
  Transaction commits on return. Steps 17
  and 18 are dispatched inside it — the stock
  alert below is deferred to AFTER_COMMIT.
end note

EP --> W : 19. STOMP broadcast
OS --> C : 20. OrderResponse
C  --> W : 21. 201 Created

AL -> AL : 22. event received
note over EP, AL
  @Async @TransactionalEventListener
  (AFTER_COMMIT) — own thread, once
  the order has committed
end note
AL -> AL : 23. handle breach
note over EP, AL
  drafts a Purchase Order if none is in flight
end note
AL -> EP : 24. stock alert

@enduml
